{
  "id": "Compound::DB08896 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Regorafenib is known to bind to Cyp2c8, a cytochrome P450 enzyme that participates in various oxidative metabolic pathways, including the oxidation of compounds such as caffeine. This binding and subsequent participation in oxidative activity are linked to Cyp3a4, which is a member of the CYP3A family and is involved in the metabolism of numerous drugs. The evidence suggests that Regorafenib may influence Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp2c8, which in turn modulates the activity of Cyp3a4. The overlapping participation of Cyp3a4 in multiple metabolic processes, as indicated by the shared participation in oxidoreductase activities, supports the notion that Regorafenib could exert a regulatory effect on Cyp3a4 via Cyp2c8. The consistent evidence across the three paths highlights a mechanistic link between Regorafenib and Cyp3a4, emphasizing the role of Cyp2c8 as a potential mediator in this relationship.",
